{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00599",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 12.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "Okay, so my sore throat is back again. It's like the fourth time since winter, and I'm honestly sick of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.51,
      "end_seconds": 20.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Four times. That's a pattern worth chasing. When did this round start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.36,
      "end_seconds": 34.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.08,
      "text": "Um, a couple of weeks ago, I guess. But it's been on and off for about two months, if you count the earlier ones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.23,
      "end_seconds": 46.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "So two months of it coming and going, with this stretch being the latest. What does it feel like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.06,
      "end_seconds": 57.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "Kind of scratchy, like I swallowed a handful of gravel. Worse when I first wake up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.47,
      "end_seconds": 63.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Gravel, got it. Anything else going on, besides the throat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.19,
      "end_seconds": 74.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "There's these lumps under my jaw. They feel like little peas, right here, on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.17,
      "end_seconds": 90.35,
      "duration_seconds": 14.18,
      "text": "Those are lymph glands. Think of them as the guard posts on the road into your head, they swell up when there's trouble in the neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.15,
      "end_seconds": 96.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Huh. That makes sense, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.14,
      "end_seconds": 102.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Have you had a fever with this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.65,
      "end_seconds": 116.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.37,
      "text": "Yeah, last week I had one, I was kind of shivery for a couple days. But that went away on Sunday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.87,
      "end_seconds": 122.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Good. Fever gone, then. Any cough with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.59,
      "end_seconds": 127.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "No, not really. Just the throat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.36,
      "end_seconds": 132.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "And is swallowing hard, like food getting stuck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.73,
      "end_seconds": 141.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "No, it hurts a little, but nothing gets stuck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.56,
      "end_seconds": 153.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Okay. Let's talk about what you're taking. What's in your medicine cabinet right now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.24,
      "end_seconds": 163.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "There's my blood pressure pill, lisinopril, 10 mg, once a day. I take it with my coffee."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.69,
      "end_seconds": 168.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Great. Anything else, even stuff from the drugstore?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.7,
      "end_seconds": 183.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.62,
      "text": "Tylenol, 500 mg, when it's bad. Probably most days, honestly. And those throat lozenges, I get through a few a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.64,
      "end_seconds": 192.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Okay. That's three things, then. Any allergies to medicines or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.52,
      "end_seconds": 199.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Nope, no allergies that I know of. I've taken everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.28,
      "end_seconds": 224.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Good. Now, I'll read your numbers. Hold still for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.55,
      "end_seconds": 233.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Temperature is 37.1 °C, and pulse is 76. Both nice and calm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.08,
      "end_seconds": 239.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "That's good, right? I felt awful this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.62,
      "end_seconds": 251.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "Numbers are a snapshot. Like checking a car's dashboard at a red light, it doesn't tell you what the engine did yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.84,
      "end_seconds": 259.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Ha, okay. So what do you think is going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.16,
      "end_seconds": 276.66,
      "duration_seconds": 15.5,
      "text": "Honestly, I can't say yet. It could be strep that keeps getting a foothold, and I can't rule that out. It might also be something viral that's lingering."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.35,
      "end_seconds": 283.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "So it's not just me being run down?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.53,
      "end_seconds": 295.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.94,
      "text": "Being run down helps these things along, but let's not guess. I'd like to do a throat swab for strep today, that's quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.46,
      "end_seconds": 300.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Is that the gagging one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.0,
      "end_seconds": 310.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Afraid so. Two seconds and a bit of an awkward face, then it's over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.89,
      "end_seconds": 316.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Great. I'll try to look dignified."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.51,
      "end_seconds": 328.54,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "And I'd also like to order a blood test to check for mono, since the glands have been swollen so long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.71,
      "end_seconds": 333.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Mono? Like, the kissing disease? I'm forty-one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.26,
      "end_seconds": 346.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "It's not only for teenagers. Plenty of adults get it, and it can drag on for weeks, which would fit your story."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.89,
      "end_seconds": 354.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Okay. Blood draw, that's fine. When do I find out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.35,
      "end_seconds": 365.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "Swab result in a day or two, bloods a bit longer. The front desk will call you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.52,
      "end_seconds": 374.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Okay. And what do I do about the throat in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.26,
      "end_seconds": 387.49,
      "duration_seconds": 12.23,
      "text": "Warm salt water, plenty of fluids, and rest. Your throat is like a sprained ankle. It heals faster if you stop walking on it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.55,
      "end_seconds": 394.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "That's hard. It's a busy week coming up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.72,
      "end_seconds": 404.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "Then take as many quiet minutes as you can steal. Even small breaks help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.01,
      "end_seconds": 411.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Fine. I'll sneak some in at lunch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.29,
      "end_seconds": 422.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in one week, to go through the results together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.0,
      "end_seconds": 429.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "One week. Okay, I'll book it at the desk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.01,
      "end_seconds": 437.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Good. And keep the Tylenol at the dose you're using, don't push past it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.67,
      "end_seconds": 440.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Right, I won't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.65,
      "end_seconds": 445.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Anything else bugging you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.9,
      "end_seconds": 454.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "Just the parking validation, I forgot to bring the ticket. Never mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.04,
      "end_seconds": 461.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "The front desk can stamp it for you on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.65,
      "end_seconds": 467.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Sounds good. Thanks, doc."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.35,
      "end_seconds": 477.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "You're welcome. Go see the nurse for the swab on your way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 478.79,
      "end_seconds": 480.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Will do. Bye."
    }
  ]
}
